{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/315070-magic-towns","id":315070,"title":"Magic Towns?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-17T21:41:29-08:00","id":315070,"title":"Magic Towns?","content":"Has White Wolf ever written about secret communities of supernatural beings? Maybe an entire town composed of only Kinfolk, Kinain, Shifters, and Changelings? Or a deep underground cave/town/Node composed of Sorcerers, Mages, and Familiars, plus maybe a few Wraiths/Risen for seasoning, where all the Tradition and Craft willworkers come to trade at the bazaar or carve a sanctum/home for themselves out of the walls so they can be next to their own kind?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T03:33:11-08:00","id":315225,"title":"","content":"Doissetep - Dark Ages Mage. But there should be more! The whole concept is awesome! Not so much as they become common but at least more than one. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2435-prophet","name":"Prophet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2435_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T06:20:20-08:00","id":315338,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\">Horizon Realms, in general.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\">Some Freeholds, I think, could be construed as their own cities (Goblin Town from </span><i>Kithbook: Nockers</i><span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\"> comes to mind). </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\">As far as \u201cSorcerers, Mages, and Familiars,\u201d most Void Engineer colonies [pre-DA] fit that description. For potential cross-splat gatherings, all friendly-like, you could repurpose the notion of </span><i>Holocaust</i><span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\">-class Voidships. I seem to remember the write up on these mentioning a few different critters - Nephandi, BSDs, Banes, Fomori, and I think Tzimisce vampires. However, that's a very...different...type of game. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\">Sounds like you\u2019re trying to combine <i>Goblin Markets</i> and the town of Midian from </span><i>Nightbreed </i><span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\">(?). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T08:02:59-08:00","id":315390,"title":"","content":"Horizon, the Stronghold of Hope<br /> <br /> There is an entire city of mages and consorts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","name":"SixFootChicken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"559"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T08:17:41-08:00","id":315392,"title":"","content":"Brainerd, MN in Fargo by Night. (OK, it was from a magazine, but still...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T12:24:34-08:00","id":315617,"title":"","content":"I can't point to any specific canon examples, but small villages of all-kinfolk sound entirely reasonable (for certain values of village). There's tons of them, they're easily guardable, they don't have any need to be around other people. Villages with large changeling populations don't seem reasonable because it's not lineaged in quite same way, and changelings thrive on having large numbers of human dreamers around. Villages of all vampires aren't do-able at all for reasons that should be obvious, and you can bet your fangs that the Garou will not tolerate them in their villages of kinfolk. Mages seem like they would get along alright, maybe even with other supers, but there's hardly enough mages to fill out a population.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2214-traveller","name":"Traveller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2214_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T17:39:58-08:00","id":315786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Traveller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/315070-magic-towns?p=315617#post315617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't point to any specific canon examples, but small villages of all-kinfolk sound entirely reasonable (for certain values of village). There's tons of them, they're easily guardable, they don't have any need to be around other people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Plus, didn't the Black Fury book say something about an isolated village where matriarchy rules?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Traveller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/315070-magic-towns?p=315617#post315617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Villages with large changeling populations don't seem reasonable because it's not lineaged in quite same way, and changelings thrive on having large numbers of human dreamers around.</div> </div> </div> </div>What are the rules for Musing Kinain? Also, its not a Changeling village so much as its a Changeling AND Kinain village. They all live together, and the Kinain probably live as Retainers with their limited ability to use Cantrips.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Traveller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/315070-magic-towns?p=315617#post315617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages seem like they would get along alright, maybe even with other supers, but there's hardly enough mages to fill out a population.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, but there are plenty of humans, and they can all use Sorcery. Mages can do their thing, and Sorcerers can do their thing. Since teaching Sorcery is something that EVERY Order of Hermes teacher is trained to do before they can begin looking for apprentices this shouldn't be a problem. They may be looking for apprentices with Avatars on the verge of Awakening, but training Sorcerers that aren't on the cusp of Awakening to act as their Retainers or Allies is probably a good idea as well. And it makes the possibility for a human run magical city feasible. It also helps to boost your Paradigm. And they might have a few Wraiths/Risen around because there are obviously going to be casualties on the part of the Magi and their friends so they can at least give them a place to rest and be castigated while they learn new Arcanoi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T18:08:50-08:00","id":315796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prophet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/315070-magic-towns?p=315225#post315225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doissetep - Dark Ages Mage. But there should be more! The whole concept is awesome! Not so much as they become common but at least more than one. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks, I saw a webcomic a while back, can't remember the name of it, that centered around a half-orc. One of the big features of the webcomic was how there was this huge underground society for all of the D&amp;D magical malcontents (all of which were some variety of evil) and I figure it would probably be something that could be pulled off on earth. A few miles beneath the surface under the ocean perhaps.<br /> <br /> Then I saw these comics,<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.charbythevampirate.com/comic/984\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.charbythevampirate.com/comic/984\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.charbythevampirate.com/comic/984\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.charbythevampirate.com/comic/984 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.charbythevampirate.com/comic/996\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.charbythevampirate.com/comic/996\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.charbythevampirate.com/comic/996\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.charbythevampirate.com/comic/996 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.charbythevampirate.com/comic/1001\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.charbythevampirate.com/comic/1001\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.charbythevampirate.com/comic/1001\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.charbythevampirate.com/comic/1001 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.charbythevampirate.com/comic/1002\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.charbythevampirate.com/comic/1002\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.charbythevampirate.com/comic/1002\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.charbythevampirate.com/comic/1002 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.charbythevampirate.com/comic/1003\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.charbythevampirate.com/comic/1003\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.charbythevampirate.com/comic/1003\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.charbythevampirate.com/comic/1003 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.charbythevampirate.com/comic/1004\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.charbythevampirate.com/comic/1004\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.charbythevampirate.com/comic/1004\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.charbythevampirate.com/comic/1004 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> and I thought about how much fun a game centered around magical beings, preferably magi since I am a fan, holed up in their own little corner of an otherwise mundane world, occasionally leaving it and bringing a bit of wonder with them into the regular world would be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 11-19-2014, 12:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T01:20:16-08:00","id":358124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/315070-magic-towns?p=315796#post315796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Thanks, I saw a webcomic a while back, can't remember the name of it, that centered around a half-orc. One of the big features of the webcomic was how there was this huge underground society for all of the D&amp;D magical malcontents (all of which were some variety of evil) and I figure it would probably be something that could be pulled off on earth. A few miles beneath the surface under the ocean perhaps. . .<br /> <br /> <br /> . . .and I thought about how much fun a game centered around magical beings, preferably magi since I am a fan, holed up in their own little corner of an otherwise mundane world, occasionally leaving it and bringing a bit of wonder with them into the regular world would be.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're looking for Dudleytown, Connecticut (detailed in <i>Freeholds and Hidden Glades</i>). Known to the fae as &quot;Graymere Glen&quot;, it was originally a nunnehi (Native American fae) site. But they abandoned it due to certain . . . &quot;difficulties&quot;. Later, Polish immigrants found tin in the area, and built Dudleytown . . . only to experience the same &quot;issues&quot;. Although, to their credit, they did hold on until the mid-Twentieth Century. <br /> <br /> You see, it takes a special kind of place to accommodate both the fae and mundane humans. And most places can't do it - too hard to balance banality against glamour. But Dudleytown wasn't most places.<br /> <br /> From the epic <i>Beowulf</i> to the <i>Friday the 13th </i>movies, people have told tales of the &quot;dark lake in the woods&quot;. A place where the willows walk . . . and something terrible dwells in the water. They're all talking about the same place. They're talking about Graymere Glen. A wise man would have stayed away. But the humans wanted the tin . . . and the lake wanted to hear them scream. <br /> <br /> Some of the newly arrived sidhe discovered the area during the Accordance War. The perfect place for a summer home, after all. Old growth forest, beautiful lake, natural source of glamour . . . the perfect retreat. <br /> <br /> The lake didn't like that idea.<br /> <br /> Some of the sidhe actually had a chance to scream. <br /> <br /> * * * * <br /> If you're looking for somewhere to set your campaign, and want to use Dudleytown, you have two options. You can go with Dudleytown during its prime (i.e. pre-1950s), before the tin ran out. Plenty of humans living and working in the area, all desperately trying to ignore what's going on around them. Not the easiest feat, considering that many of the local chimera can step into &quot;mundane&quot; reality, at least for a moment or two . . .<br /> <br /> Or, in the modern day, you can look at Cornwall, the neighboring town. Nowadays, Dudleytown is almost a ghost town (inhabited by a couple changelings and chimera born of an entire town gone mad), but its so etched in the local imagination, <i>things</i> can occasionally wander through the woods to &quot;visit&quot;. Even most of the changelings of Graymere Glen actually live in Cornwall. Not that they're afraid of their own freehold, you understand. . . . <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}